{
 "note": "Words that name a genus, in the languages our leads are written in. Read by scripts/refill.py to recover a genus from a tree's OWN NAME, which is the commonest missing field in data/leads/ and the one that keeps a fully verified tree out of the writable pile.",
 "why_genus_only": "A name says Eiche, never Quercus petraea, so this can only ever reach the genus. CLAUDE.md's 2026-08-13 ruling is exactly this case: write 'Oak (Quercus sp.)', say on the page that we do not know which one, and let a reader answer it. Genus from the tree's own name is a reading of the name, not a guess about the tree.",
 "not_a_publish_decision": "This fills LEADS, never data/cities. A lead becoming writable is not a tree going live: a write pass still looks at it.",
 "how_to_grow": "Add words to an existing genus, or a new genus with a common name. Re-run refill.py; it is idempotent.",
